CAT = "rotxDriver"; SEG = "DRV"
Q = [
("What is the minimum age to drive a taxi or a rental car with driver in Romania?",
 "21", ["18", "23", "25"],
 "Law 38/2003, art. 26, requires taxi and rental drivers to be at least 21 years old."),
("For how long must a taxi driver have held a category B licence?",
 "At least 2 years", ["At least 1 year", "At least 3 years", "At least 5 years"],
 "Art. 26 requires a valid category B licence held for at least two years."),
("Which document proves a driver is professionally trained for taxi or rental work?",
 "The ARR attestation", ["A driving school diploma", "A town hall work permit", "A taxi union membership card"],
 "The certificate of professional attestation (certificat de atestare profesională) is issued by the Romanian Road Authority (ARR) and is required for both taxi and rental drivers."),
("Which ARR office issues a driver's taxi attestation certificate?",
 "The agency where they work", ["Any office the driver picks", "The Bucharest head office only", "The office in their birth county"],
 "Art. 26 says the certificate is issued by the ARR agency for the area in which the driver carries out the activity."),
("Before applying for the taxi attestation, a driver must complete:",
 "A driving school course", ["An internship with the police", "A degree in transport", "A year as a bus driver"],
 "The professional training is given by an authorised driving school on an ARR-approved programme, and proof of finishing the course is needed for the ARR test."),
("How long is the professional training course for taxi or rental attestation?",
 "30 hours", ["10 hours", "60 hours", "120 hours"],
 "The training norms (Annex 7^1 to Order 1214/2015 as amended) set the course at 30 hours, covering law, customer service, taxi practice, driving and safety, and security."),
("A taxi driver must be fit from which points of view?",
 "Medical and psychological", ["Financial and fiscal", "Academic and linguistic", "Physical and sporting fitness"],
 "Art. 26 requires a driver to be medically and psychologically fit, proved by medical and psychological approvals for passenger transport."),
("A criminal conviction for which kind of offence bars a person from driving a taxi?",
 "An offence against property", ["An unpaid parking fine", "A late personal tax return", "A neighbour's noise complaint"],
 "The criminal record must show no conviction for offences against road safety, drugs, life and health, trafficking of vulnerable people, sexual freedom and integrity, or property."),
("The police certificate needed for the course must show that in the last year the driver had no:",
 "A suspension for drink or drugs", ["Unpaid parking tickets", "A change of home address", "Speed camera photo warnings"],
 "Art. 27 asks for a traffic police certificate showing no suspension in the last year for driving under alcohol or drugs and no accident with victims caused by the driver."),
("For how long is a taxi driver's attestation certificate issued?",
 "With no end date", ["For one year only", "For three years", "For ten years"],
 "The certificate is issued for an indefinite period, but it is valid only if it is endorsed (vizat) every five years (Law 38/2003, art. 28)."),
("How often must a taxi driver's attestation certificate be endorsed (vizat)?",
 "Every 5 years", ["Every year", "Every 2 years", "Every 10 years"],
 "Art. 28 makes the five-yearly endorsement compulsory; at endorsement the driver must also prove medical and psychological fitness and hold a suitable licence."),
("Where in Romania may a driver work on a valid taxi attestation certificate?",
 "Anywhere in Romania", ["Only in the issuing county", "Only in Bucharest", "Only in the home town"],
 "The certificate is valid throughout Romania. The taxi itself still works under the authorisation of one locality."),
("At a roadside check, a taxi driver must show the attestation certificate:",
 "When inspectors ask", ["Only at the town hall", "Only once a year", "Only after a crash"],
 "Art. 52(3)(b) requires the driver to hold a valid attestation and show it on request to the control bodies named in the law."),
("A driver of a car in rental mode (închiriere) must hold the attestation and also be:",
 "Employed by the carrier", ["The owner of the car", "Registered with a dispatcher", "A member of a taxi chamber"],
 "Art. 25 says the rental driver must hold the professional attestation and be an employee of the authorised carrier."),
("An individual taxi carrier (persoană fizică) may hand their taxi to another taxi driver:",
 "Never, for contracted rides", ["Only at night, when quiet", "For up to a week at a time", "If the other driver is attested"],
 "Art. 52(2)(d) forbids an individual or family association carrier from handing over the driving of the taxi to another taxi driver to perform the contracted service."),
("A carrier may not use as a taxi driver someone who:",
 "Has no attestation", ["Speaks only Romanian", "Lives in another town", "Drives a brand-new car"],
 "Carriers may not use drivers without a professional attestation or who have serious breaches in their professional conduct record."),
("The occupational standard that sets good practice for taxi drivers is called:",
 "The taxi driver's standard", ["The national road safety charter", "The fiscal procedure code", "The urban mobility plan"],
 "Art. 52(3)(a) refers to the occupational standard for taxi drivers (Standardul ocupațional al taximetristului), on which the course's customer-care topics are based."),
("When several drivers share one taxi in a day, each starts work by:",
 "Using an electronic key", ["Signing the dispatcher's book", "Calling the town hall", "Resetting the meter to zero"],
 "Art. 46 says each driver identifies themselves to the taxi meter with an electronic key, which also lets their own work be checked."),
("When working out a taxi driver's effective working time, which pauses are left out?",
 "Breaks of over 15 minutes", ["Every stop at traffic lights", "All time spent at a taxi stand", "The first hour of each shift"],
 "Law 38/2003 defines effective working time from the start of the first ride to the end of the last, without pauses over 15 minutes between rides while the taxi stood still."),
("Taxi drivers' working time must also respect the rules on:",
 "Driving and rest periods", ["Shop opening hours", "Local school term dates", "Public holiday road timetables"],
 "Art. 2 requires respect for Government Ordinance 17/2002 on driving and rest periods and the organisation of working time in road transport."),
("A taxi driver must dress and behave towards clients:",
 "Neatly and politely", ["As the client asks", "In any way off duty", "Only as the carrier sets"],
 "Art. 52(3)(a) requires appropriate dress and civilised, preventive behaviour towards clients, following good practice."),
("A taxi driver may use the car's radio for an alarm only when:",
 "There is a real emergency", ["Traffic is very slow", "A booked client is late", "The meter shows Free"],
 "Drivers must not use the radio for unjustified alarms that could disturb public order; in justified critical situations they may send an emergency call."),
("A taxi driver who witnesses a serious incident must inform:",
 "The police, quickly", ["The dispatcher only", "The client's family", "Nobody, unless asked"],
 "Art. 52(3)(h) requires the driver to tell the police as soon as possible, and with priority, about any serious event they took part in or witnessed."),
("A taxi driver must never knowingly use the taxi for:",
 "Criminal activity", ["Night rides", "Rides to the airport", "Card payments"],
 "Art. 52(3)(g) forbids involving the taxi deliberately, directly or indirectly, in criminal or other antisocial acts."),
("A driver's licence was suspended for drink driving eight months ago. Can they join a taxi course now?",
 "No, a full year must pass", ["Yes, straight away", "Yes, with a lawyer's letter", "Only for rental work"],
 "The traffic police certificate needed for the course must show no suspension for alcohol or drugs in the last year, so the driver must wait until a year has passed."),
("When endorsing the attestation, the driver must also prove they hold:",
 "A suitable driving licence", ["A university degree", "A second paid job", "A share in the carrier's company"],
 "Art. 28 says the certificate stays valid if it is endorsed on time and the driver proves medical and psychological fitness and holds a suitable licence."),
("Is a taxi driver's attestation also needed to drive a car in rental mode with driver?",
 "Yes, the same rule applies", ["No, any B licence is enough", "Only for airport rides", "Only for foreign clients"],
 "Art. 26 sets the same conditions, including a valid attestation, for both taxi transport and transport in rental mode."),
("Which document about the driver's past must be presented to join the training course?",
 "A criminal record certificate", ["A secondary school report", "A reference from a bank", "A history of past addresses"],
 "Art. 27 lists the application, licence copy, criminal record certificate, ID, medical and psychological approval and the police certificate among the course documents."),
]
